Do not wait for a pixel-by-pixel specification.

I specifically want you to make the design decisions.

Audit the existing UI and determine where its hierarchy, density, proportions, typography, navigation, feedback, component consistency, spacing, information architecture, interaction patterns, and visual rhythm can be improved.

Then redesign it as a unified system.

Do not simply preserve every existing layout and repaint it with darker colors.

At the same time, do not arbitrarily change game rules or remove information that players need.

The goal is to improve how Seren communicates the game, not to simplify it by hiding important mechanics.

