* display/title typography
* navigation/actions
* normal explanatory copy
* compact metadata
* numerical/readout information

Typography should contribute heavily to Seren's professional character.

Preserve localization requirements. The interface must work cleanly in both English and French, including strings that become longer after translation.

Do not hard-code layouts that only work for the current English copy.

## Responsive behavior

Seren must continue to work across its existing target environments.

The redesign must be intentional on:

* portrait phones
* landscape phones
* desktop browsers
* tall/narrow desktop windows
* large displays
* local split-screen configurations

